 "signals_basis": "attempts that obtained the signal-ledger lock (the ledger file), plus lock-timeout refusals that the signalling process reported (``unrecorded``). A signaller that ended before it could report (for example a Successor stopped by the backstop) may have made further refused attempts that cannot be counted: the counts are a lower bound on attempts. ``delivered`` counts RECORDED deliveries (kill(2) returned success and the entry was appended): the ledger entry is written after kill(2), so a signaller that died between the two may have delivered a signal that is not recorded, and delivered is a lower bound too. kill(2) success is acceptance by the kernel, not an effect on the target.",
